  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The&nbsp;Williamson&nbsp;ether&nbsp;synthesis&nbsp;is the most widely used method to synthesize ethers. It occurs by an <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math> reaction in which a metal alkoxide displaces a halide ion from an alkyl halide.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mtext>RO</mtext><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mtext>R</mtext><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>-</mo><mtext>x</mtext><munder><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mtext>S</mtext><mtext>N</mtext></msub></munder><mtext>R</mtext><mo>-</mo><mtext>O</mtext><mo>-</mo><msup><mtext>R</mtext><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math><br /><br />This is Nucleophilic substitution reaction.</p></blockquote>",
